{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:53e6ae3801655c5e337cf62307a1f7a9494524fe","text":"Retired because it is not a review, despite reading as one.\n\nI wrote the body with `status: approved`. The fold makes a report a review only when `body.verdict` is set (fold.go: `state.Kind == KindReport \u0026\u0026 state.Body[\"verdict\"] != \"\"`), and `gs merge` checks `approval.Body[\"verdict\"] != \"approved\"`. So this report is an effective statement that projects as no review at all, and merging on it would have been refused. The `gs review` command builds `{\"verdict\", \"head\", \"artifact\"}` and cannot make this mistake; filing the same act through the MCP `state` tool can, and did.\n\nThe judgement is unchanged and the head is unchanged. A correctly bodied approval follows. Nothing rests on this report, so retiring it cascades to nothing."}